*~
.DS_Store
**/project.xcworkspace/
**/xcuserdata/
build/

# Rust wrapper crate (rust/, tests/*.rs). Cargo.lock isn't committed: this
# is a library crate, and library crates leave version resolution to their
# consumers rather than pinning it here.
target/
Cargo.lock

# Corpus fixtures are regenerated locally via build_corpus_apps.sh — not
# committed. corpus_apps/ contains extracted fragments of real third-party
# app binaries (not ours to redistribute); corpus_files.txt/
# corpus_files_apps.txt are manifests of machine-specific absolute paths.
corpus_apps/
corpus_files.txt
corpus_files_apps.txt

# libFuzzer's working corpus: generated, machine-specific, and grows without
# bound. fuzz/build/ is already covered by the build/ rule above. If a run
# ever produces coverage worth keeping, minimize it (`-merge=1`) into a small
# committed seed directory rather than committing this one. Crash reproducers
# (crash-*, timeout-*) SHOULD be committed if found — they are regression
# tests, not artifacts.
fuzz/corpus/

